The image view's per-file 3D entries are the stereo layer's menu, "3D Input Format", shown through the layer's QML
form (Stereo.FileChoiceMenu, stereo-layer 1.19.0), and its choices are kept in the layer's per-file store, the one
Dolphin, the thumbnailers and Gwenview read (ORDER 551b; Daniel, 2026-10-23: "never touch the user file"). A picture
set to Not 3D or given a packing in Dolphin or Gwenview opens that way here, the menu shows what the store holds, and
a choice made here shows there. The file is written only by the layer's "Save the correction into the file".

The input packing, the anaglyph pair, Not 3D and the swap of the eyes were one choice for every picture of the
view, kept for the session; they are now each file's own. Nothing Koko offered is gone: the layer's menu holds
Automatic, Not 3D, side by side and top and bottom in either order, the anaglyph pairs and the swap, and adds the
interleaved packings, picture and depth and the save into the file. "Anaglyph to side by side" stays, with its notice
on colour, and keeps the pair for the file. Stereo, Left eye only and Right eye only stay in the 3D menu as this
view's own choice. The shortcuts keep working: Alt+Shift+3 opens the menu, Alt+Shift+W swaps the eyes of the picture
shown, Alt+Shift+N switches Not 3D for it, Alt+Shift+D, L and O choose the view.

A picture shown flat is offered no swap and no save. A file's choice follows it when it is renamed or moved through
the desktop's file jobs; a copy carries nothing.

The sentences the 3D menu keeps are in German and Spanish too.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.19.0.
